Z||000000||pHoOl||10-27-2001||01:50 PM||||Went to honk at a car the other day, and found that it wasn't workin.  I've never really dug into the horn before, and considering how cold and windy it is outside, dont' want to spend any more time than i have to.<P>I'm assuming the horn is placed up front, i think i've seeen it by the front facia.  I'm gonna check for wires.  Where is the fuse located for the horn?  I checked the set of fuses under driver side dash, but didn't see the one for horn there.  I don't have my owners manual (back at home 150 miles away) so i'm bound to asking for help here.  <P>I was having problems with the switch before where soemtimes the horn would start goign while i was driving.  Just had to hit the horn to fix it when it happened, but it makes me wonder if maybe the switch finally bit the dust.  I don't think it did, because when i hit the horn now, i dont' here the beep, but still hear the click from the passenger side under dash.<P>Thanks for help!<BR>I feel kinda dumb asking for help on how to fix a horn, but it's all good<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||10-27-2001||02:19 PM||||My horn didn't work the 1st time I went to use either.  It was the switch/button on the steering wheel.  The genius mechanic that the previous owner brought the car to strikes again!  They had assembled the switch wrong after replacing the spring in upside down.  This may not be your problem if was working before.  GL||||reg||1
